\ GBA notes
\ 32-bit ARM v7 TDMI, 16.78MHz (roughly 60ns each) (Thumb support)
\ Little-endian

\ Not targeting an interactive system on the GBA; rather this is using the
\ metacompiler to target the GBA with a game.

\ See gba/DESIGN.md for most of the details!


\ Entry point for metacompiling the portable kernel to ARM 32-bit for the GBA.
\ Most of the heavy lifting is done in other files, this is just orchestrating.

REQUIRE ../host/vocabularies.ft

host definitions

\ Metacompiler configuration =================================================
host REQUIRE ../host/configuration.ft

rom-application!

8    config char-bits    !
4    config cell-width   !
4    config instr-width  !

config little-endian?   ON


\ Target spaces ==============================================================
REQUIRE ../host/spaces.ft

\ For the GBA, the name space is not present on the target.
\ The data space is separate and starts empty, because it's in a separate RAM.
REQUIRE header.ft

\ The header goes at the start of the file and the start of ROM at $08000000.
\ It's 192 bytes long, so the code section can start right after it.

\ The 256B in IWRAM at $03007f00 to $03007fff are reserved for the interrupt
\ vector, interrupt stack and BIOS call stack.
\ There's 32KB of IWRAM, and I want a handful of tasks to fit into it.
\ Reserving 2KB for the interrupt bits, global VARIABLEs and miscellany, that
\ leaves 30KB for tasks. 30KB would give:
\ - 40 tasks 192 cells
\ - 32 tasks 240 cells
\ - 16 tasks 480 cells

\ We'll allow for variable-sized tasks in any case.

\ Make the generic Forth data space be the fast one and track how big it gets.

\ Multiple ROMs and metacompilation ==========================================
\ How to control which data space Forth stuff is going to?
\ The `data-there` is a VALUE, so it can be updated with TO.

$40000 THERE-PTR ewram
$8000  THERE-PTR iwram

$02000000 ewram space>org !
$03000000 iwram space>org !
ewram blank-space!
iwram blank-space!

iwram TO data-there \ Let the main globals go here.


\ XXX: START HERE: Figure out the right spaces and their ORGs.
\ Also make sure the DUMP logic understands that the names should only be
\ written when has-dictionary? is set.
\ Code space goes in ROM and data space in IWRAM.
\ Code space goes at 0 in the output, but $08000000.

\ Data and name spaces don't go in the output file! (-1)
\ However, data space exists in IWRAM at runtime.
-1      $03000000 0          THERE-PTR data-there
-1      0         name-space THERE-PTR name-there


REQUIRE assembler.ft

\ The QEMU ARM system starts executing user code at $10000.
\ We need to assemble at that location, then
$10000 org!

host REQUIRE ../host/helpers.ft
host REQUIRE model.ft
host REQUIRE ../host/dictionary.ft
host REQUIRE ../host/mirrors.ft

\ Now we have what we need to metacompile the CODE definitions at the heart of
\ the new kernel.
host REQUIRE kernel.ft

\ Overwrite the jump target of the entry point at $10000 to be main.
there @   $10000 there !
main b,
there !

\ The main part of the metacompiler
host REQUIRE ../host/metacompiler.ft

\ Now an interleaved dance of shared and target-specific metacompiled code.
host REQUIRE ../shared/basics.ft
host REQUIRE branches.ft               \ Target-specific branching helpers.
host REQUIRE ../shared/control-structures.ft
host REQUIRE ../shared/exceptions.ft
host REQUIRE model-target.ft
host REQUIRE ../shared/input.ft
host REQUIRE ../shared/core2.ft
host REQUIRE ../shared/refill.ft
host REQUIRE lib.ft                    \ Division etc. helpers
host REQUIRE serial.ft
host REQUIRE terminal.ft
host REQUIRE ../shared/output.ft
host REQUIRE ../shared/error-messages.ft
host REQUIRE intro.ft
host REQUIRE ../shared/init.ft         \ Shared init code.

host definitions
VARIABLE output-file-xt
:noname S" forth-arm.bin" ; output-file-xt !

\ NB: You should always include tail.ft as the last stage of your build.
\ It actually emits the assembled image.

\ Known-missing words ========================================================
\ Core: ENVIRONMENT? WORD
